DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The iissssppaaccee() and iissssppaaccee__ll() functions test for white-space characters.
     For any locale, this includes the following standard characters:

     ``\t''   ``\n''    ``\v''    ``\f''    ``\r''    `` ''

     In the "C" locale, iissssppaaccee() and iissssppaaccee__ll() return non-zero for these
     characters only.  The value of the argument must be representable as an
     _u_n_s_i_g_n_e_d _c_h_a_r or the value of EOF.

     The iissssppaaccee__ll() function takes an explicit locale argument, whereas the
     iissssppaaccee() function uses the current global or per-thread locale.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     The iissssppaaccee() and iissssppaaccee__ll() functions return zero if the character
     tests false and return non-zero if the character tests true.

